\title{rdz: Fast Serialization of R Objects}
\description{
Provides a native serialization path for common R vectors, lists, matrices, and data frames. String vectors adapt between dictionary and flat layouts. An optional balanced preset dictionary-encodes low-cardinality numeric vectors with bit-packed and optionally LZ4-compressed indexes, packs logical vectors into two bits per value, packs small-range integer offsets, and stores exact constant-delta numeric sequences compactly. High-cardinality doubles can use an exact XOR-delta and byte-transpose transform with independent LZ4 blocks when it saves at least 12.5 percent. High-cardinality strings adapt between flat LZ4, positional byte transposition, and prefix/suffix coding using a bounded first-block selector. String lengths use run-length encoded metadata when smaller. Unsupported objects automatically fall back to R's general serialization format.
